  "query_preview": "..\nZonal flow aloft remains in place across the region until \nWednesday. The EC/GFS and NAM all break down the zonal flow with\na amplifying 500 mb trough over the west coast with a compact \nvorticity center for forcing, lifting across the WA Cascades and\nColumbia Basin around Wednesday Night. This pattern influence \nwould impact temperatures, bring moisture some mid levels \nmoisture and increased risk for thunderstorms to the WA Cascade \nCrest as well as induce gusty winds to the Gap areas. \n\nWith the incoming upper wave Wednesday afternoon and Night, \nincreasing probabilities for precipitation accompany the \ninherent lightning risk. NBM mean QPF ranges from around one \ntenth of an inch up to about one half inch across the East \nWashington central and northern Cascades and western Methow \nValley. Lesser amounts are forecast across the Okanogan \nHighlands/Kettle Mountains and Selkirk Mountains. HeatRisk is \nlimited this week for all areas east of the Cascades, primarily \naffecting those who are extremely sensitive to heat and without \ncooling or hydration.",
